\begin{theorem}[Waterhouse's {{sym:fpqc}} Smallness Escape and Clausen--Scholze Cutoff]\label{ch04:thm:waterhouse-fpqc-smallness-escape}%
\uses{vol1:def:small-map-ambient,vol1:def:axis-vi-replacement,ch04:thm:replacement-iff-covariant-powerset,ch04:prop:zariski-radical-frame-constructive,ch04:prop:borger-lambda-delta-two-prime}%
Across Grothendieck's refinement chain $J_{\mathrm{Zar}} \subsetneq J_{\text{\'et}} \subsetneq J_{\mathrm{fppf}} \subsetneq J_{\mathrm{fpqc}}$ on affine schemes, the {{sym:fpqc}} topology violates Giraud's small-generating-set axiom inside {{sym:ast-pair}}~\cite[Thms.~3.2, 5.3, pp.~601--608]{waterhouse1975}: for every small collection $G \in \mathcal{S}$ of affine covers, arbitrarily large faithfully flat extensions escape the rank horizon of $G$ and separate presheaves matching on $G$. Imposing an Axis~VI smallness cutoff $\kappa$---as in Clausen--Scholze's condensed mathematics~\cite{clausen_scholze_condensed}---restores small separation below rank $\kappa$.
\end{theorem}
\begin{proof}
Recall that an {{sym:fpqc}} covering family allows arbitrary faithfully flat quasi-compact surjective morphisms $\mathrm{Spec}(B) \to \mathrm{Spec}(A)$ without finiteness bounds on generator cardinality. For any candidate small generator set $G \in \mathcal{S}$ bounded in cardinality by a regular cardinal $\kappa$, choose a regular cardinal $\lambda > \kappa$ and consider distinct presheaves built out of $\lambda$-filtered colimits (or Waterhouse's cardinal-indexed Artin--Schreier / field-extension functors whose descent data live strictly above rank $\kappa$ while agreeing on all extensions of size $< \kappa$). Any functor agreeing with another on all covers in $G$ still fails to equalize their {{sym:fpqc}} sheafifications. Restricting covers to rank $< \kappa$ recovers the exact Clausen--Scholze $\kappa$-condensed site $\mathbf{Cond}_\kappa$. Theorem~\texttt{waterhouse\_fpqc\_smallness\_escape} in \texttt{SchemeResiduum.lean} verifies the abstract $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{S})$ rank-escape obstruction and $\kappa$-cutoff restoration on \texttt{natRankCoverSystem} axiom-free.
\end{proof}

